# CraftBench .gitattributes — line-ending and binary-asset guard
#
# Why this file exists: a Windows checkout with git's default
# core.autocrlf=true rewrites LF -> CRLF in tracked text at checkout time. For
# most files that is harmless. For the three kinds below it is not, so their
# bytes are pinned on every platform.
#
# Scope is deliberately narrow. There is NO blanket `* text=auto`: a text
# guess applied to the committed binary UE maps and assets would re-normalize
# and corrupt them, and the committed binary is the only map source — a
# mangled .umap is an explicit L2 FAIL.

# --- The project descriptor: read and rewritten by the runner ---
# The runner edits the cloned workdir's .uproject (plugin disable) and writes
# it back with explicit \n. Pinning it LF keeps that byte-stable across OSes
# and keeps cross-platform diffs clean.
*.uproject text eol=lf

# --- POSIX shell entry points: CRLF breaks bash on the \r ---
# The repo-root `cb` shim and setup.sh execute under sh/bash on macOS, Linux
# and git-bash; an autocrlf checkout injects \r into every line including the
# shebang, and the script dies with an unreadable error.
/cb      text eol=lf
setup.sh text eol=lf
*.sh     text eol=lf

# --- UE binary content: never normalize, never diff as text ---
# 109 .umap + 658 .uasset are committed binaries. `binary` disables eol
# conversion AND text diffing, so neither autocrlf nor a text=auto guess can
# ever rewrite their bytes.
*.umap   binary
*.uasset binary
